WHAT THIS PROJECT IS

A reproduction of the screening method described in "Designing Agentic AI-Based
Screening for Portfolio Investment" (arXiv:2603.23300). The paper's authors are
credited in README.md. A method is not copyrightable, so that citation is an
attribution owed to their work rather than a licensing condition on this code.


THE BUNDLED MARKET DATA

The published container image contains a prebuilt DuckDB database at
/opt/agentic-portfolio/data/portfolio.duckdb, covering 2015-01-02 to 2024-04-29.
It is bundled so that the paper's backtest can be reproduced without a
multi-hour rebuild, and because the window is fixed history that cannot go stale.
Its exact contents, row counts and build date are recorded beside it in
DATASET.json.

It is derived from three sources, with three different positions:

  U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission (EDGAR) - the book-equity figures.
  Public domain. EDGAR is subject to the SEC's fair-access policy, which
  requires a descriptive User-Agent and rate limiting; this project honors both
  (see src/agentic_portfolio/dataset/sec_edgar.py and the SEC_UA setting).

  Wikipedia - the S&P 500 membership list and its historical changes.
  Licensed CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/) and
  attributed here as required. Source:
  https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_S%26P_500_companies

  Yahoo Finance - the price, dividend and split history.
  Yahoo's terms of service restrict redistribution of their data. This project
  bundles it anyway, deliberately and for one narrow purpose: non-commercial
  reproduction of a published academic result. That is a considered decision and
  not an oversight, and it is recorded as such in
  plans/20_packaging_and_release.md's Decision Log.

If you would rather not rely on our copy - whether for licensing comfort, or
because you want current data, or because you simply want to verify it - build
your own and point the DB_PATH environment variable at it. Every step is a
first-class command of this tool:

  portfolio-build-membership
  portfolio-build-prices
  portfolio-build-fundamentals      # needs SEC_UA
  portfolio-build-momentum
  portfolio-build-returns
  portfolio-build-dividends
  portfolio-build-news-archive

Nothing in this software requires the bundled database. The user_provided
selection, the holdings report, and the whatif explorer all fetch what they need
on demand and never read it.


NO INVESTMENT ADVICE

This is research software that reproduces an academic method. Its output is not
a recommendation, the historical figures it reports are not a prediction, and
the dividend figures it computes are a record of what was paid rather than a
promise of what will be.
